			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Modularize Window namespace factories for OutputChannel, Status Bar, Terminal, and Webviews\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Window/Namespace.ts` implementation into distinct factory modules: `CreateOutputChannel`, `CreateStatusBarItem`, `CreateTerminal`, `CreateWebviewPanel`, and `CreateWebviewViewBuilder`. This refactoring aligns the VSCodeAPI handler suite with the project's strict PascalCase directory hierarchy and separation of concerns principles.\n\nThe new modules implement the full VS Code extension host API surface for window interactions, bridging Cocoon-side mutations to Mountain via gRPC notifications:\n- **OutputChannel**: Bridges `append`/`log`/`dispose` calls, forwarding channel names to support `dev_log` tagging in Mountain for Git/SCM diagnostics.\n- **StatusBarItem**: Implements `show`/`hide`/`dispose` with snapshot-based updates for `text`, `tooltip`, and `command`.\n- **Terminal**: Adds lazy `processId` resolution with promise caching to prevent RPC spam in hot loops, plus `sendText`, `resize`, and visibility controls.\n- **WebviewPanel & WebviewView**: Implements full lifecycle management including `html` setters, `postMessage`, CSP handling, visibility state, and event listeners (`onDidChangeViewState`, `onDidDispose`). The `WebviewView` specifically fixes `visible` getter initialization to prevent React mount short-circuiting in extensions like Roo.\n\nThis change eliminates inline factory logic from the namespace file, reducing cognitive load and enabling unit testing of individual UI component proxies.",
			"SHA": "8f1737b2f232d186e3efdaba78ab03f8e0c7077c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T20:06:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1122,
				43
			],
			"Message": "build(Cocoon): Regenerate build artifacts and RouteManifest\n\nRe-run the TypeScript compilation and ESBuild bundling pipeline to update the `Target/` directory with the latest source state. The `RouteManifest.ts` report is updated with a new generation timestamp reflecting the current build cycle.\n\nAll compiled JavaScript bundles and their corresponding source maps are regenerated to ensure the extension host binary matches the updated source hierarchy. This maintains consistency across the dependency graph, including the gRPC client, VSCodeAPI handlers, and Mountain integration layers.",
			"SHA": "10a6451f10b7ffbb1aa0f7a4621e0e3dc2fd785e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T19:56:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				1122,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Complete PascalCase directory hierarchy migration\n\nFinalize the restructuring of the Cocoon source tree and build artifacts to enforce the strict PascalCase directory hierarchy. This commit moves all remaining flat-named files (e.g., `BaseConfig.js`, `Constant.js`, `TypeConverter.js`) into nested directories where every logical segment of the path becomes a distinct PascalCase folder (e.g., `Config/Base/Config.js`, `Constant/Environment/Constant.js`).\n\nUpdate ESBuild configuration imports, service interfaces, and the comprehensive VSCodeAPI handler suite to reflect the new file locations. Regenerate the `RouteManifest.ts` to include new Webview and Debug method counts, and update `README.md` documentation to link to the new paths. Regenerate all `Target/` build artifacts to ensure the compiled extension host bundle resolves imports correctly against the new structure.\n\nThis change completes the migration initiated in previous commits, ensuring consistent organization across the entire extension host codebase.",
			"SHA": "8e2bfa404f9a232ca9ca1c43feaecb0e5aaa22b4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:40:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				958,
				109
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Update import paths to match PascalCase directory hierarchy\n\nFollowing the recent restructuring of the Cocoon source tree into a strict PascalCase directory hierarchy, update all internal import paths to reflect the new file locations. This affects the Bootstrap entry point, Codegen tools, ESBuild configuration modules, Effect services, IPC message handling, and the comprehensive VSCodeAPI handler suite.\n\nSpecifically, update references to split compound filenames (e.g., `TypeConverter.ts` to `Type/Converter.ts`, `PostHogBridge.ts` to `Post/Hog/Bridge.ts`) across the entire module graph. Also remove the deleted `RouteManifest` generated files which are now handled differently. Ensure all relative paths resolve correctly to the new nested directory structure.",
			"SHA": "fbbd8c0ea2db4716f27acaa6d805c4381e2d4c7f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:40:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				961,
				121
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Standardize file structure with PascalCase directory hierarchy\n\nMigrate the entire Cocoon source tree from flat file naming to a strict PascalCase directory hierarchy, splitting compound names (e.g., `IConfigurationService.ts` becomes `I/Configuration/Service.ts`) into nested folder structures. This affects all core modules including Bootstrap, Codegen, Configuration, Effect, IPC, Interfaces, Services, TypeConverter, and Utility.\n\nThe refactoring enforces the project's naming conventions where every logical segment of a path is a distinct PascalCase directory, ensuring consistent organization across the extension host codebase. All file moves are content-preserving (similarity index 100%), requiring no code logic changes but necessitating updates to import paths throughout the module graph. This restructuring aligns with the architectural pattern established in recent commits regarding ESBuild configuration and service standardization.",
			"SHA": "41d2f5d1d3c4221a1262e9f64e04bc94627ab385"
		}
